{
  "case_id": "2008-08-205",
  "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Theodore B. Olson",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Robust debate about candidates for elective office is the most fundamental value protected by the First Amendment's guarantee of free speech. Yet that is precisely the dialogue that the government has prohibited if practiced by unions or corporations, any union or any corporation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Olson, are you taking the position that there is no difference in the First Amendment rights of an individual? A corporation, after all, is not endowed by its creator with inalienable rights. So is there any distinction that Congress could draw between corporations and natural human beings for purposes of campaign finance?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Do you think Congress could prevent foreign individuals from funding speech in United States elections?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Olson -- Mr. Olson, would you answer Justice Ginsburg's question yes or no? Can the -- leaving aside foreign investors, can the -- can -- does the First Amendment permit any distinction between corporate speakers and individual speakers?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Isn't that what happened in Buckley?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Yes, but that point wasn't even discussed in the opinion, was it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what was discussed in the opinion was the breadth of the definition of \"person,\" which did include corporation. Corporations were parties in the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think you are wrong about the consequence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Senator Mitch McConnell",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0001-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first case cited to you by Mr. Olson happened to be New York Times v. Sullivan, and I would like to begin by urging two propositions on you from that case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kagan",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have three very quick points to make about the government position. The first is that this issue has a long history."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "NRA",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "and which is argued by the NRA, an appropriate answer to this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "question we have posed on reargument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But if you -- if you insist on the as-applied challenge, isn't that inconsistent with the whole line of cases that began in Thornhill v. Alabama and Coates v. Cincinnati?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: One of the amicus briefs objects to -- responds to Justice Kennedy's problem by saying that the problem is we have got to contribute to both parties, and a lot of them do, don't they?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ask, it seems -- to your shareholder protection rationale, isn't it extraordinarily paternalistic for the government to take the position that shareholders are too stupid to keep track of what their corporations are doing and can't sell their shares or object in the corporate context if they don't like it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Olson",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My point is that the government here has an overbroad statute that covers every corporation irrespective of what its stockholders think, irrespective of whether it's big, and whether it's general -- a big railroad baron or anything like that, and it doesn't know, as it stands here today two years after this movie was offered for -- to the public for its view, what media might be covered, what type of corporation might be covered and what compelling justification or narrow standard would be applied to this form of speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "94f4f182fc37801d08a6456d91b45c287c738c2924833fa1f145a91f73c94dfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-94f4f182fc37-0004-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-08-205",
      "confidence": 0.0,
